    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "137f2c1a-e028-3504-a7a9-fdc6cf89f976",
                "word": "knothole",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e197cb39-8512-48a2-ac5f-a76700a6aeb1",
                        "entry_id": "137f2c1a-e028-3504-a7a9-fdc6cf89f976",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "knotholes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b7566f8e-1ab9-3b20-8910-54efac480e86",
                        "entry_id": "137f2c1a-e028-3504-a7a9-fdc6cf89f976",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a piece of lumber, a void left by a knot in the wood; such holes are often convenient for peering through when they occur in fences."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "49412ab0-ae67-40fd-8592-c11c46c52908",
                                "sense_id": "b7566f8e-1ab9-3b20-8910-54efac480e86",
                                "text": "Looking in the same direction, I saw that the knothole in the wall had indeed become a human eye -- a full, black eye, that glared into my own with an entire lack of expression more awful than the most devilish glitter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0020fa25-645f-4179-98a0-a24dec191362",
                                "sense_id": "b7566f8e-1ab9-3b20-8910-54efac480e86",
                                "text": "These city-owned parks, regal concrete crowns with acres of parking lots and nary a knothole to peek through, are a definite swing away from the democratic character of the earlier ballparks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "298bd369-3c25-4cb7-9872-36e1ef28a01a",
                                "sense_id": "b7566f8e-1ab9-3b20-8910-54efac480e86",
                                "text": "Besides, there's an old saying: peek not through a knothole, lest ye be vexxed."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "960f767d-86e9-3e27-8883-f88e8765f7ef",
                        "entry_id": "137f2c1a-e028-3504-a7a9-fdc6cf89f976",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Youth league baseball."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Cincinnati",
                            "attributive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e5c2eff-3f13-4b98-94c2-c9630d5f6dd3",
                                "sense_id": "960f767d-86e9-3e27-8883-f88e8765f7ef",
                                "text": "But he was worried that a coach of a knothole team might not like the idea and not let me switch-hit. So, my dad went to the coach."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ce7abd5-0999-484e-8b6a-447a4c73e364",
                                "sense_id": "960f767d-86e9-3e27-8883-f88e8765f7ef",
                                "text": "I was a Cub Scout. I went to church with my family, and taught Sunday school when I was in my teens. I played knothole baseball and rooted for the Reds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bc590062-c3b0-4e8e-a976-007e0fbf2a26",
                                "sense_id": "960f767d-86e9-3e27-8883-f88e8765f7ef",
                                "text": "Poetically enough, the New Richmond knothole field is situated right next to the low, open land between the old and new highway."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f664cd4-68f3-4e88-a7ae-2e1ce37daecc",
                                "sense_id": "960f767d-86e9-3e27-8883-f88e8765f7ef",
                                "text": "In 1955 members organized their first baseball league; softball and knothole baseball were added later."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b6e91f4f-a841-4179-b0b0-d4abd9f02077",
                        "source_entry_id": "137f2c1a-e028-3504-a7a9-fdc6cf89f976",
